assistant: Subject: parse epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Since vendor API version 2026-10-01, `/orders/{id}` sends `created_at` as a number of milliseconds since 1970 (e.g. `1792142857943`) instead of an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` ran `Date.parse(String(...))` on it. That returned NaN, the `|| 0` fallback turned it into 0, and the tool reported 1970-01-01 without any error. The fix in `src/tools/get_order.ts` uses a numeric `created_at` directly as epoch milliseconds and still parses string values as before, so the 2026-01-01 version is unaffected. With that change the repro test, the contract tests and the v1 fixture tests all pass, and so do typecheck and lint. The tool sends the same requests as before.

